"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead and an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One. The project has progressed through several stages: it began with a kick-off in June, followed by a call for R&D ideas in July to leverage AI for data visualization. In September, the team expanded with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing. By October, the project reached a major milestone with a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing, and the focus shifted to user interface enhancements. Strategic partnerships were established with TechInnovate, an AI research leader. In November, the team reported a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for a staff meeting on November 20th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, the project is moving into a development phase led by Omar Jensen, following the completion of the design phase."
